Embodied AI Safety Guardrails showcases high-risk instruction recognition, action interception, permission control, and safety responses via an on-site robot.
When a task violates safety policies, the robot halts execution and provides voice/screen alerts. The backend visualizes the entire process: recognition, risk assessment, policy matching, and interception:
High-Risk Action Recognition;
Unauthorized Instruction Interception;
Physical Environment Constraints;
Human-Robot Interaction Safety Alerts;
Execution Log Retention & Traceability.

Fangcun AI Frontier LLM Safety Evaluation Report (White Paper) showcases systematic safety evaluation for frontier LLMs, covering cybersecurity, biochemical safety, loss of control, model deception, and Agent behavioral risks:
Frontier Risk Evaluation Framework;
Automated Red-Teaming Processes;
Multi-Dimensional Risk Scoring;
Model Behavioral Analysis;
Automated Safety Report Generation.
The report highlights Fangcun AI’s research depth and engineering expertise, proving its vital value in global advanced AI safety research.

It showcases explainable AI capabilities for understanding LLM internal mechanisms, highlighting SAE-based feature extraction, concept activation, and risk signal identification.
Visitors can compare models and input custom prompts to see key features, semantic concepts, and risk signals triggered inside the model. Using graphs and activation paths, it demystifies the black box decisions:
Safety Alignment Variance (Aligned vs. Unaligned);
Internal Model Feature Visualization;
Semantic Concept Activation Analysis;
Risk Feature Identification;
Black-Box Mechanism Explanation.

